### E. Public Grid Builder

This is the main feature of the website.

Allow users to create custom Formula 1 grids with exactly 10, 11, or 12 teams.

Each constructor has two primary driver seats.

#### Grid configuration

- Grid name.
- Season year or alternate-season label.
- Team count: 10, 11, or 12.
- Constructor selection for every team.
- Driver selection for both seats.
- Optional custom constructor names for fictional teams.
- Optional custom team colors and logos where permitted.
- Save, duplicate, edit, and delete custom grids.
- Reset grid with a confirmation dialog.
- Preview the complete lineup.
- Export the finished grid as a poster.

#### Driver assignment interface

Build a polished visual editor with:

- Team cards.
- Constructor logo.
- Team name.
- Driver 1 and Driver 2 slots.
- Driver portraits.
- Driver names and codes.
- Searchable driver selection modal.
- Drag-and-drop assignment on supported desktop devices.
- Accessible dropdown-based assignment on all devices.
- Clear and replace seat actions.
- Immediate visual updates when assignments change.

#### Validation rules

- The same driver cannot occupy multiple seats within the same lineup.
- A constructor cannot be duplicated within a lineup by default.
- Users can optionally enable duplicate constructors for fictional scenarios.
- Each standard constructor has exactly two seats.
- Incomplete grids can be saved as drafts.
- A grid can be marked complete only when all required seats are filled.
- Changing a seat must immediately update the preview.
- Validation must happen in both the client and server/database layer where applicable.

Allow fictional constructors, historical pairings, and driver transfers across alternate seasons.

Do not restrict custom lineups to official real-world pairings.

