## 7. Supabase Database Schema

Create migrations for the following tables.

### `teams`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `name text not null`
- `slug text unique not null`
- `logo_url text`
- `hq text`
- `bio text`
- `primary_color text`
- `secondary_color text`
- `created_at timestamptz`
- `updated_at timestamptz`

### `team_cars`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `team_id uuid references teams(id)`
- `year integer not null`
- `car_name text`
- `car_image_url text`
- `wins integer default 0`
- `poles integer default 0`
- `podiums integer default 0`
- `points numeric default 0`
- `created_at timestamptz`
- `updated_at timestamptz`

Enforce uniqueness on `(team_id, year)`.

### `drivers`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `name text not null`
- `code text unique not null`
- `nationality text`
- `bio text`
- `card_image_url text`
- `podium_image_url text`
- `grid_image_url text`
- `created_at timestamptz`
- `updated_at timestamptz`

### `seasons`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `year integer`
- `name text not null`
- `season_type text`
- `is_current boolean default false`
- `is_published boolean default false`
- `created_at timestamptz`
- `updated_at timestamptz`

Use a separate stable season identifier so fictional seasons with labels or multiple variants are not forced into a single unique calendar year. Define appropriate uniqueness rules for the chosen season model.

### `driver_team_seasons`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `driver_id uuid references drivers(id)`
- `team_id uuid references teams(id)`
- `season_id uuid references seasons(id)`
- `seat_number integer`
- `created_at timestamptz`
- `updated_at timestamptz`

Enforce unique driver assignment within a season and unique constructor seat within a season.

### `custom_lineups`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `created_by uuid references auth.users(id)`
- `name text not null`
- `season_id uuid references seasons(id)`
- `team_count integer not null`
- `status text`
- `visibility text`
- `created_at timestamptz`
- `updated_at timestamptz`

### `custom_lineup_teams`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `lineup_id uuid references custom_lineups(id)`
- `team_id uuid references teams(id)` nullable when the user creates a fictional constructor
- `custom_team_name text`
- `custom_logo_url text`
- `custom_primary_color text`
- `position integer not null`

Enforce unique positions within each lineup.

### `custom_lineup_seats`

- `id uuid primary key`
- `lineup_team_id uuid references custom_lineup_teams(id)`
- `driver_id uuid references drivers(id)`
- `seat_number integer not null`

Enforce one driver per seat and prevent duplicate drivers within the same lineup using an appropriate database constraint or transaction-safe database function.

### `admin_roles`

- `user_id uuid primary key references auth.users(id)`
- `role text not null`
- `created_at timestamptz`

Only trusted administrators may grant or modify admin roles.

Add foreign keys, indexes, validation constraints, timestamps, and update triggers as appropriate. Use database migrations to keep schema changes version-controlled.

