## 9. Security and Authorization

Implement production-grade security.

- Enable RLS on every table exposed through the Supabase API.
- Public users may read only published and intentionally public content.
- Administrators may manage teams, drivers, cars, seasons, assignments, and media.
- Authenticated users may create and manage their own private lineups.
- Users may update only their own lineups unless an explicitly authorized administrator action applies.
- Public lineup reads must respect visibility.
- Verify administrator privileges through a trusted database-backed role or secure authorization function.
- Do not rely on hidden buttons or frontend routes for security.
- Do not place a Supabase service-role or secret key in frontend code.
- Use the publishable key in the client with appropriate RLS policies.
- Add rate limits or abuse controls where appropriate.
- Sanitize user-provided text and validate all inputs.
- Use transactions or database functions for multi-record lineup updates and uniqueness validation.
- Add appropriate error logging without exposing secrets or private user information.

Generate a complete RLS policy migration and verify access using both anonymous and authenticated test accounts.

